---
title: Pasta con Ceci
description: Pasta and chickpeas cooked together in one pot, with the tomato paste fried in garlic oil first.
tags: [pasta, one-pot]
course: main
icons: [pot-food, tomato, garlic]
cuisine: Italian
difficulty: easy
author: Victoria Granof
source:
  name: Food52
  url: https://food52.com/recipes/66790-victoria-granof-s-pasta-con-ceci
servings: 2
prep time: 5m
cook time: 25m
---

In a large heavy-bottomed #pot{}, heat the @extra-virgin olive oil{4%tbsp}(plus more for drizzling) until it shimmers.

Add the @garlic cloves{3}(peeled and smashed) and cook, stirring, until lightly browned and fragrant.

Stir in the @tomato paste{3%tbsp}(good) and @kosher salt{1%tsp}(or more to taste) and fry for ~fry{30%seconds} or so.

Add the @chickpeas{1 1/2%cup}(cooked, or one 15-oz can, drained and rinsed), @ditalini pasta{1/2%cup}(uncooked, or another small shape, like macaroni), and @boiling water{2%cup}.

Stir to scrape up any browned bits on the bottom of the pot, lower the heat, and simmer until the pasta is cooked and most of the liquid has been absorbed, about ~simmer{15-20%minutes}. Taste and adjust the seasoning.

To serve, ladle the pasta into shallow bowls, sprinkle with @red pepper flakes{}, and drizzle a bit of @&extra-virgin olive oil{} on top.
